Cross-compile driver 
--------------------

To cross-compile, you will need a compiled kernel to build against.

To compile the driver, make sure your cross-compiler is in your PATH.

Then build the driver:

(Update ARCH, CROSS_COMPILE and KERNEL_SRC as appropriate)

    make MORSE_TRACE_PATH=`pwd` ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-linux-gnueabihf- KERNEL_SRC=~/linux CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_MORSE=m CONFIG_MORSE_SDIO=y CONFIG_MORSE_USER_ACCESS=y

MM6108 monitor transmission
---------------------------

With CONFIG_MORSE_MONITOR enabled, the monitor netdev accepts raw 802.11ah
management and data frames when the module parameter
`enable_monitor_injection=1` is set. It defaults to off. The radio must be in
monitor mode with a valid channel selected. This path is limited to MM6108
SoftMAC firmware and does not add control-frame, encryption, or TX status
support.

Frames need a radiotap header followed by an 802.11ah frame. Supported TX
controls are the S1G radiotap TLV (one spatial stream, MCS, bandwidth,
guard interval, and PPDU format), the Morse frequency TLV, and basic
radiotap flags, channel, rate, and retry fields. Unsupported TX controls
and frames outside the selected operating channel or regulatory range are
dropped. The monitor netdev TX counters reflect firmware queue acceptance,
not confirmed over-the-air delivery.

